---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
const updated = "5 July 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the kirpik.app website and the Kirpik text protection app for Shopify handle data. Operated by INFOWISE LIMITED."
>
  <PageHero title="Privacy Policy" />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>
      <p>
        This policy covers two things: this website (kirpik.app) and the
        Kirpik text protection app for Shopify. Both are operated by
        {SITE.developer}.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The kirpik.app website is a static site. It has no accounts, no
        sign-up forms, no analytics scripts and no advertising or tracking
        cookies. We do not collect personal information from visitors.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site-check tool on this site runs entirely in your browser. The
        store address you enter is used by your own browser to look up
        publicly available pages, and it is not transmitted to us or stored by
        us. As with any website, the infrastructure providers that host and
        serve kirpik.app process network requests, such as IP addresses, as a
        normal part of delivering pages.
      </p>

      <h2>The Kirpik app: what we process</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Store information.</strong> Your Shopify store domain, your plan, and the settings you configure in the app, including your store's watermark code.</li>
        <li><strong>Protected content records.</strong> When you protect a product description, blog article or page, the app processes that text to embed the watermark. We do not keep a copy of your full original text. We store SHA-256 content fingerprints, bounded excerpts, word counts and timestamps, which are what detection and certificates need.</li>
        <li><strong>Detection records.</strong> When you run a detection, we record the result, including the URL you checked or an excerpt of the text you pasted, detection details and timestamps, so that results can be reviewed and certificates generated.</li>
        <li><strong>Proof of Ownership Certificates.</strong> Certificates you generate, together with the public verification pages that back them, contain the details described on the certificate itself.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing.</strong> Subscriptions are handled by Shopify through Shopify Managed Pricing. We see your plan status. We never receive or store your payment card details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide the service: protecting content, running detections, restoring content and generating Proof of Ownership Certificates.</li>
        <li>To operate, secure and improve the app, including debugging, rate limiting and abuse prevention.</li>
        <li>To respond when you contact support.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell data. Information is shared only with the
        infrastructure providers required to run the service, for example
        hosting, the managed fetching service used for URL checks, and the
        Internet Archive when building certificate timelines, and where the
        law requires it. Proof of Ownership Certificates and their verification
        pages are documents you generate and choose to share for your own
        enforcement purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep store settings, protection records and detection records while
        the app is installed, so that protection can be reversed and past
        detections and certificates remain verifiable. After you uninstall,
        associated data is deleted or anonymised in line with our retention
        schedule and our obligations under Shopify's data requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or
        delete personal data we hold. Email
        <a href="mailto:support@kirpik.app">support@kirpik.app</a> and we will
        deal with your request.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions go to {SITE.developer} at
        <a href="mailto:support@kirpik.app">support@kirpik.app</a>, or through
        the support form inside the app.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
